{"name":"Pitter Patter","hex":"#9bc2bd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pitter-patter","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A soft, percussive sound, as of tiny feet, or of rain on a rooftop; patter."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To patter; to scurry."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pitter-patter"}],"entries":[{"title":"M.I.U. Album","blocks":[{"text":"M.I.U. Album is the 22nd studio album by the American rock band the Beach Boys, released on September 25, 1978 by Brother/Reprise. Characterized for its easy-listening sound, the album was produced by Al Jardine and touring member Ron Altbach during one of the most acrimonious periods in the band's history. It sold poorly, peaking at number 151 in the U.S., and was met with confused reactions from critics and fans."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/68/MIUCover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/M.I.U._Album"},{"title":"Patter","blocks":[{"text":"Patter is a prepared and practiced speech that is designed to produce a desired response from its audience. Examples of occupations with a patter include the auctioneer, salesperson, dance caller, magician, and comedian."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patter"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/MUM_campus_and_tower.jpg/500px-MUM_campus_and_tower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/MUM_campus_and_tower.jpg/1280px-MUM_campus_and_tower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/MUM_campus_and_tower.jpg/500px-MUM_campus_and_tower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Maharishi International University in Fairfield, Iowa, where most of M.I.U. Album was recorded","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMUM_campus_and_tower.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Brian_Wilson_1977.jpg/500px-Brian_Wilson_1977.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Brian_Wilson_1977.jpg/500px-Brian_Wilson_1977.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Brian Wilson (pictured 1977) was reported to be \"miserable\" throughout the M.I.U. sessions and had resented collaborating with Mike Love on most of the album's songs.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABrian_Wilson_1977.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/The_Beach_Boys_Konzert_Michigan_1978_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-The_Beach_Boys_Konzert_Michigan_1978_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/The_Beach_Boys_Konzert_Michigan_1978_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-The_Beach_Boys_Konzert_Michigan_1978_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/The_Beach_Boys_Konzert_Michigan_1978_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-The_Beach_Boys_Konzert_Michigan_1978_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Beach Boys performing a concert in Michigan, August 1978","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Beach_Boys_Konzert_Michigan_1978_(cropped).jpg"}],"sounds":{"pitter-patter":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4a/En-us-pitter-patter.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/4/4a/En-us-pitter-patter.ogg/En-us-pitter-pa